      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Luckey since 1881, marking the village’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luckey%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1881, builders finished a hotel, stave factory, sawmill, and lime kiln, turning the settlement into a bustling lumber center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.luckeyohio.org/historyluckeyohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "From 1949 to 1958, a nearby production site manufactured beryllium for the U.S. Atomic Energy Commission, linking Luckey to national defense.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luckey%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2019, First Solar’s new float glass plant began construction just outside Luckey, the first new glass plant in the U.S. since 1980.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luckey%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
